questions.question_text:
Diagnose and resolve an asynchronous state race condition in a React component (Core JavaScript/TypeScript & Browser Runtime).

### Defective Code:
```javascript
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
function UserProfile_1({ userId }) {
    const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
    useEffect(() => {
        // Defect: Race condition on rapid userId change and missing unmount cleanup
        fetchUser(userId).then(data => setUser(data));
    }, [userId]);
    return <div>{user?.name}</div>;
}
```

### Reported Anomaly / Error:
Stale props race condition: if userId updates from 1 to 2 rapidly, response 1 can resolve after response 2, overwriting state with stale data in Core JavaScript/TypeScript & Browser Runtime.

Identify the root cause of the defect and provide the corrected code snippet with rationale.

questions.correct_answer:
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
function UserProfile_1({ userId }) {
    const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
    useEffect(() => {
        let isCurrent = true;
        fetchUser(userId).then(data => {
            if (isCurrent) setUser(data);
        });
        return () => { isCurrent = false; };
    }, [userId]);
    return <div>{user?.name}</div>;
}

